  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social rights, health and social security: EJP support and administration</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project supports programme-wide activities of the 4th phase of the Economic Justice Programme, including financial management and administration. The project will contribute to the reduction of social and economic inequality and poverty in Brazil by defending and promoting access, especially of the poorest, to the Brazilian social security system (this covers free universal basic healthcare, social insurance and social assistance which includes pensions, unemployment, maternity, child and disability benefits etc) which is guaranteed in the 1988 Constitution and which is crucial in tackling extreme poverty and socioeconomic exclusion of a large part of the population. Local and national advocacy and networking will hold public authorities to account to ensure that social policies and programmes are properly resourced and benefit the poor. Project activities include: training of local community leaders to understand how the health, social insurance and social security systems work, and preparing them with skills, information and know-how to be able to influence public authorities in meetings and audiences; coordination and networking with other organisations at local and national level to influence and hold public authorities to account to defend and better implement policies; and capacity strengthening of programme partners in monitoring, planning and communication.</narrative>
  </description>
